.TH FUNES 1 "September 2026" "funes" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
funes \- clipboard history that never forgets
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B funes
.RI [ COMMAND ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Funes
is a keyboard-first clipboard manager for X11 desktops, built with Python,
GTK 3 and libxapp. It records everything copied to the CLIPBOARD selection,
keeps a searchable history, and pastes the selected entry back into the window
that was focused before its popup opened.
.PP
Running
.B funes
with no command starts the tray daemon. Only one instance runs at a time;
further invocations are delivered to it over D-Bus and start it if needed.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B toggle
Show or hide the history popup. This is the command bound to the global
shortcut.
.TP
.B show
Show the history popup.
.TP
.B clear
Clear the history. Pinned items are kept.
.TP
.B settings
Open the settings window.
.TP
.B quit
Stop the running instance.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH POPUP KEYS
.TP
.B type
Filter the history (case-insensitive substring match).
.TP
.BR Up ", " Down
Move the selection;
.BR PageUp / PageDown
move ten rows.
.TP
.B Enter
Copy the selected entry and paste it into the previously focused window.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Enter
Copy only, without pasting.
.TP
.B Ctrl+P
Pin or unpin the selected entry. Pinned entries are never evicted.
.TP
.B Delete
Remove the selected entry.
.TP
.B Ctrl+L
Clear the history, keeping pinned entries.
.TP
.B Escape
Close the popup.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings live in GSettings under the
.B org.x.funes
schema and can be changed with the settings window, the
.BR gsettings (1)
command or
.BR dconf-editor (1).
Notable keys:
.TP
.B history-size
Maximum number of unpinned entries (default 200).
.TP
.B hotkey
Global shortcut that toggles the popup (default <Super>v). On Cinnamon it is
registered automatically as a custom keybinding running "funes toggle".
.TP
.B paste-on-select
Inject the paste keystroke after copying (default true).
.TP
.B paste-ctrl-v-class-regex
Windows whose WM_CLASS ("res_name.res_class") matches this regular expression
are pasted with Ctrl+V instead of Shift+Insert.
.TP
.B ignore-regexes
Clipboard text matching any of these regular expressions is never stored.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/funes/history.db
SQLite history database, created with mode 0600. It is not encrypted.
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/org.x.funes.desktop
Autostart entry, managed by the
.B launch-at-login
setting.
.SH NOTES
Entries advertised as password-manager secrets
(x-kde-passwordManagerHint, org.nspasteboard.ConcealedType) are never stored.
Under Wayland, keystroke injection only reaches XWayland clients, so
paste-on-select is disabled.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gsettings (1),
.BR dconf-editor (1)
